    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d708">

                <pb facs="0593" n="477" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg477"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/11633b.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Consul Canada.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-04-21T04:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 21, 1914, 4 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Fletcher has been instructed to take the customhouse immediately and prevent
                    delivery of arms and ammunition. Confer with Fletcher. This despatch is sent as
                    a matter of precaution for fear the despatch sent directly to him might be
                    delayed. Immediate action necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
